From 8fd88a098054b421d57cef6fa00023f55f4f6a3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iggy <iggy@triform.ai>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 03:33:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cloud-browser: add webrtc_overrides passthrough for
 cloud-browser
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds //third_party/webrtc_overrides/cloud_browser/BUILD.gn — a thin
passthrough source_set whose only job is to re-export the webrtc
public-API targets that //cloud-browser/* needs, via public_deps.

Why this patch exists:
- Chromium's rtc_library template enforces visibility on every webrtc
  internal target: only //third_party/webrtc/* and
  //third_party/webrtc_overrides/* may depend on them. cloud-browser
  is in neither, so direct deps from //cloud-browser/* are rejected
  by gn check.
- The chromium-canonical fix is a passthrough source_set inside
  webrtc_overrides — that path IS in the visibility list, so it can
  depend on webrtc internals and re-export them as public_deps.
- public_deps (vs deps) propagates header visibility to dependents,
  so consumers don't need to know which specific webrtc subtarget
  owns each header.

Targets re-exported:
- api/units:data_rate                   (webrtc::DataRate)
- api/video:encoded_image               (webrtc::EncodedImage)
- api/video:video_bitrate_allocation    (webrtc::VideoBitrateAllocation)
- api/video:video_frame                 (webrtc::VideoFrame, I420Buffer)
- api/video_codecs:video_codecs_api     (VideoEncoder, EncoderFactory,
                                          SdpVideoFormat, VideoCodec)
- modules/video_coding                  (CodecSpecificInfo, h264_globals,
                                          video_codec_interface, error_codes)
- rtc_base:logging                      (RTC_LOG)

Touched file:
- third_party/webrtc_overrides/cloud_browser/BUILD.gn  (new file, +41 lines)

Resolved against branch-heads/7727 (Chromium 147 stable).
---
 .../webrtc_overrides/cloud_browser/BUILD.gn   | 38 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 third_party/webrtc_overrides/cloud_browser/BUILD.gn

diff --git a/third_party/webrtc_overrides/cloud_browser/BUILD.gn b/third_party/webrtc_overrides/cloud_browser/BUILD.gn
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..5f11be7a38
--- /dev/null
+++ b/third_party/webrtc_overrides/cloud_browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Copyright 2026 The Cloud Browser WebRTC Authors. All rights reserved.
+#
+# Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
+# found in the LICENSE file.
+
+# Passthrough overrides for cloud-browser (//cloud-browser/*).
+#
+# Chromium's `rtc_library` template restricts visibility on every webrtc
+# internal target to:
+#   [ //third_party/webrtc/*, //third_party/webrtc_overrides/* ]
+#
+# This file lives inside webrtc_overrides/, so it CAN depend on those
+# internals; cloud-browser depends on this passthrough's `public_deps`
+# instead, which re-exports the headers transitively. Add a new entry
+# here whenever cloud-browser's encoder/capturer code needs another
+# webrtc public-API target.
+#
+# Cross-references:
+#   * //cloud-browser/capture/build-integration/BUILD.gn  (consumer)
+#   * //cloud-browser/capture/encoder/                    (where the
+#                                                          types are
+#                                                          referenced)
+
+import("//build/config/features.gni")
+
+source_set("webrtc_api_passthrough") {
+  # public_deps so the headers + their transitive types are visible to
+  # any //cloud-browser/* target that depends on us.
+  public_deps = [
+    "//third_party/webrtc/api/units:data_rate",
+    "//third_party/webrtc/api/video:encoded_image",
+    "//third_party/webrtc/api/video:video_bitrate_allocation",
+    "//third_party/webrtc/api/video:video_frame",
+    "//third_party/webrtc/api/video_codecs:video_codecs_api",
+    "//third_party/webrtc/modules/video_coding",
+    "//third_party/webrtc/rtc_base:logging",
+  ]
+}
